win|succeed-in-competition|VERB|Succeed in a competition|To finish a competition or contest ahead of the other participants.|thắng; chiến thắng|Their team won the final match by a single point.|Đội của họ thắng trận chung kết với cách biệt một điểm.|Win, won, won; win a match, but beat an opponent. Can be intransitive: our team won.|0
win|gain-a-prize-or-support|VERB|Gain a prize or support|To obtain something through success, effort or persuasion.|giành được|The young designer won a prize for her folding chair.|Nhà thiết kế trẻ giành được một giải thưởng cho chiếc ghế gấp của cô ấy.|Transitive; win a prize, win support. Win something from someone differs from beating that person.|1
win|victory|NOUN|Victory|A successful result in a contest or competition.|chiến thắng|The narrow win kept the village team in the tournament.|Chiến thắng sát nút giúp đội của làng tiếp tục thi đấu trong giải.|Countable; a win, two consecutive wins. Victory is a more formal alternative.|2
content|information-in-a-work|NOUN|Information in a work|The ideas, information or material contained in a text, programme or other work.|nội dung|The editor checked the content of the booklet before it was printed.|Biên tập viên kiểm tra nội dung cuốn sách nhỏ trước khi in.|Usually uncountable in this use; educational content. Contents can mean the items inside a container or a book's section list.|0
content|satisfied-with-situation|ADJECTIVE|Satisfied with a situation|Satisfied with what one has or with the present situation.|hài lòng; mãn nguyện|She was content with a quiet evening at home.|Cô ấy hài lòng với một buổi tối yên tĩnh ở nhà.|Content with something or content to do something; usually after a linking verb. The adjective has final-syllable stress.|1
fridge|refrigerated-storage-appliance|NOUN|Refrigerated storage appliance|An appliance that keeps food and drinks cold.|tủ lạnh|Put the remaining soup in the fridge after it has cooled.|Hãy cho phần súp còn lại vào tủ lạnh sau khi nó đã nguội.|Countable; a fridge. Informal shortening of refrigerator; a freezer keeps things frozen rather than merely cold.|0
instrumental|important-in-achieving-result|ADJECTIVE|Important in achieving a result|Playing an important part in bringing about a result.|có vai trò quan trọng; góp phần then chốt|The librarian was instrumental in starting the reading club.|Thủ thư có vai trò then chốt trong việc thành lập câu lạc bộ đọc sách.|Instrumental in plus noun or -ing; often after be. Does not mean that someone acts as a musical instrument.|0
instrumental|music-without-vocals|ADJECTIVE|Music without vocals|Played on musical instruments rather than sung.|không lời; dành cho nhạc cụ|An instrumental version of the song played during the interval.|Một bản nhạc không lời của bài hát được phát trong giờ nghỉ.|Before a musical noun: instrumental music, instrumental version. A noun instrumental can name such a piece.|1
nowadays|at-the-present-period|ADVERB|At the present period|During the current period, often contrasted with an earlier time.|ngày nay; hiện nay|Nowadays, visitors reserve their seats online rather than at the gate.|Ngày nay, du khách đặt chỗ trực tuyến thay vì tại cổng.|One word; often at sentence start or end. Normally refers to a present habit, not one event happening this minute.|0
